PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core issue is ROMM=ProPhoto RGB (D50, very wide gamut) vs sRGB (D65, narrow triangle). ROMM primaries G(0,1,0) and B(0,0,1) lie outside sRGB; any positive linear combination on the GB edge also yields negative sRGB coords after Bradford transform and is therefore inexpressible by any 8-bit sRGB hex. Thus 1,2,3 cannot; 4 and 5 fall inside after conversion.  
Colleagues split: gamut-aware group (10,3,6,8) correctly flags 1-3; precision-only group (11,2) wrongly cites 1/255 steps and ignores gamut; “direct map” group (1,5,7,9,13,14) ignores both gamut and matrix.  
No unresolved math; consensus on primaries + edge mixture settles answer as “1, 2, 3”.}

